**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests`

**How to implement.** The start screen's view: New kit…, Open kit…, the status, the offer, the filter box and the history list, every control under a stable id (001 §F 'Start-screen actions', 'History': each row shows the name, folder, last-open date and the star; a filter box; a missing folder shows greyed, with Locate… / Remove from history; 001 §O 'Automation': ids such as `KitHistoryList`, `KitHistoryStarToggle`, `NewKitButton`; .spec-md §10.5: an opposing pair shares a row, with a gap and distinct positive and negative colours; AGENTS.md: never a wrapping `TextBlock` inside a horizontal `StackPanel`). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: a new group after the launcher group (`UiIds.fs:588`), `// --- The kit start screen (KitStartView, KitStartWindow). ---`, each member with a one-line doc: `newKitButton` (`"NewKitButton"`), `openKitButton` (`"OpenKitButton"`), `kitStartStatusText` (`"KitStartStatusText"`), `kitStartOfferText` (`"KitStartOfferText"`), `makeThisAKitButton` (`"MakeThisAKitButton"`), `openKitReadOnlyButton` (`"OpenKitReadOnlyButton"`), `cancelKitStartOfferButton` (`"CancelKitStartOfferButton"`), `kitHistoryFilter` (`"KitHistoryFilter"`), `kitHistoryList` (`"KitHistoryList"`); and, over a row's place in the list (`ConstructorUiPosition`, 0 first), `kitHistoryRow` (`KitHistoryRow_<n>`), `kitHistoryStarToggle` (`KitHistoryStarToggle_<n>`), `kitHistoryLocateButton` (`KitHistoryLocateButton_<n>`), `kitHistoryRemoveButton` (`KitHistoryRemoveButton_<n>`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type KitHistoryEntry with member this.lastOpenedCaption : ControlCaption` is `Last opened <yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm> UTC`, the time in the invariant culture as `KitLockHolder.describe` writes one (step 129); and `type KitFolder with member this.notAKitCaption : ControlCaption` is `<the folder's text> holds no kit.`. (3) `KitStartView.fs`: `kitStartView (m : KitStartModel) (dispatch : KitStartMsg -> unit) : IView`, a pure projection of the model. Its content scrolls as the material editor's does (`MaterialEditorView.fs:twoPane`: a `ScrollViewer` over a `MinWidthPanel`, `WindowLayout.fs:MinWidthPanel`), both scroll bars `Auto` and a minimum width of 520, over one vertical `StackPanel` holding, in order: (a) one row with `New kit…` (`newKitButton`) and `Open kit…` (`openKitButton`), each a `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` (public since step 107, the shared look), whose presses call `m.context.picker.pickThen` (step 174) with `CreateKit >> dispatch` and `OpenKit >> dispatch`; (b) when `status` is `Some`, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `kitStartStatusText` in `MaterialsWindowView.messageColor`; (c) for `MakeKitOffer folder`, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `kitStartOfferText` with `folder.notAKitCaption`, and under it one horizontal row of `MaterialsWindowView.actionButton`s: `Make this a kit` (`makeThisAKitButton`, `positiveBackground`, sending `CreateKit folder`) and `Cancel` (`cancelKitStartOfferButton`, `negativeBackground`, sending `DismissKitStartOffer`); for `ReadOnlyKitOffer (folder, holder)` the text is `holder.openElsewhereCaption` (step 173) and the pair is `Open read-only` (`openKitReadOnlyButton`, positive, sending `OpenKitReadOnly folder`) and `Cancel` (the same id and message, negative); the action box's right margin is the gap; (d) a `TextBox` carrying `kitHistoryFilter`, watermark `Filter kits by name or folder`, its text `m.filter.value`, sending `KitHistoryFilter >> FilterKitHistory` on each change (the `CategoryControls.fs:106` shape); (e) a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `kitHistoryList`, one row per item of `m.rows` at its position `n`: a `DockPanel` whose right side holds a `verbButton` carrying `kitHistoryStarToggle n`, labelled `★` for a starred kit (sending `UnstarKit`) and `☆` otherwise (sending `StarKit`), and, for a missing folder only, `Locate…` (`kitHistoryLocateButton n`, its press calling `m.context.picker.pickThen` with `fun found -> dispatch (LocateKit { missing = <the row's folder>; found = found })`) and `Remove from history` (`kitHistoryRemoveButton n`, sending `ForgetKit` of the row's folder); and whose fill is a `Border` carrying `kitHistoryRow n`, keyed by its id as `verbButton` keys its box, holding three `TextBlock`s: the kit's name (semi-bold), the folder's text (wrapping) and `lastOpenedCaption`. A present row's `Border` sends `OpenKit` of its folder when pressed; a missing row's `Border` has `Opacity` 0.5 and sends nothing, its two buttons staying at full opacity. Every press handler sets `e.Handled` as `verbButton` does, and every id is an AutomationId, never a `Name`, as `MaterialsWindowView.fs:verbButton`'s doc says of variable membership. (4) Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs`, `module KitStartWindowTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Its screens are mounted as `ScrollExtentTests.fs:constructorWindow` mounts a view: a `HostWindow` running `Program.mkSimple` over a model, `updateKitStart` and `kitStartView`, shown headless at 900 × 700. Its context holds an in-memory history holding `KitStartTests`' five entries (step 176) over the present folders `C:/kits/a`, `C:/kits/c` and `C:/kits/d`, an import context over `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy`, a picker `TestAppScope.kitPickerOf` of the fact's folder (step 154) and a recording `showKit`; every kit it records is closed at the fact's end. Facts without a trait: `the kit start screen UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the nine fixed ids' texts, and the four positional ids' texts at positions 0 and 3. `the history rows show name, folder and last open in display order, each with its star`: the rows at positions 0 to 4 are `d`, `b`, `c`, `a`, `e`, each `kitHistoryRow n` holding its name, its folder's text and its `lastOpenedCaption` (`Last opened 2026-11-03 12:07 UTC` for `d`), and `kitHistoryStarToggle n` reads `★` for `d` and `b` and `☆` for the rest. `a missing folder's row is greyed with Locate and Remove from history, and a present row offers neither`: rows 1 and 4 (`b`, `e`) have `Opacity` 0.5 and both `kitHistoryLocateButton n` and `kitHistoryRemoveButton n`; rows 0, 2 and 3 have `Opacity` 1 and neither. `each offer shows its text with its two buttons on one row, Cancel to the right`: over the model with `MakeKitOffer` of a test-local folder, `kitStartOfferText` reads its `notAKitCaption`, and `makeThisAKitButton` and `cancelKitStartOfferButton` have equal tops, Cancel's left beyond Make this a kit's right; over `ReadOnlyKitOffer` with step 173's holder the text is its `openElsewhereCaption`, and `openKitReadOnlyButton` and `cancelKitStartOfferButton` sit the same way. `typing into the filter box narrows the list`: setting `kitHistoryFilter`'s text to `kit c` leaves one row, `c`, and clearing it lists five. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing a box at its centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` does: `pressing a row's star, its Remove from history and a present row sends StarKit, ForgetKit and OpenKit`: pressing `kitHistoryStarToggle 3` (`a`) stars `a` in the store and pressing the `kitHistoryRemoveButton` of `e`'s row removes `e`; and, over a screen whose history holds one entry of a kit the fact made through `openKitAt` and closed (its folder present), pressing `kitHistoryRow 0` records that kit shown once. `New kit and Open kit open the folder the picker answers`: over a screen whose picker answers a fresh folder, pressing `newKitButton` records one shown kit named for it; over one whose picker answers a folder holding only `notes.txt`, pressing `openKitButton` records nothing and shows `kitStartOfferText`.

**Acceptance.** After the view lands, `kitStartView` MUST show New kit…, Open kit…, the status, the offer with its pair on one row, the filter box and one row per listed kit with its name, folder, last open and star, a missing folder's row greyed with Locate… and Remove from history, every control under its `ConstructorUiId`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing a row's star, its Remove from history and a present row sends StarKit, ForgetKit and OpenKit` and `New kit and Open kit open the folder the picker answers`, the count rising by 2; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the kit start screen UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the history rows show name, folder and last open in display order, each with its star`, `a missing folder's row is greyed with Locate and Remove from history, and a present row offers neither`, `each offer shows its text with its two buttons on one row, Cancel to the right` and `typing into the filter box narrows the list`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass.
